          "blueprint_node": "a00J01:B6",
          "status": "answered",
          "node": "a00J01:B6",
          "quote": "The measure on \\([0,1]\\) is a probability measure, hence\n\\(\\lVert g\\rVert_n\\le\\lVert g\\rVert_p\\) whenever \\(p\\ge n\\); combining this\nwith B5 and the almost-everywhere equality of \\(f\\) and \\(g\\) gives\n\\(\\alpha\\le\\lVert f\\rVert_p\\) for every \\(p\\ge n\\).",
