        {
          "question": "upper-bound-exponent-range",
          "blueprint_node": "a00J01:B2",
          "status": "answered",
          "node": "a00J01:B2",
          "quote": "Restricted Lebesgue measure on \\([0,1]\\) has total mass \\(1\\), so\nexponent monotonicity with \\(p\\le\\infty\\) gives\n\\(\\lVert f\\rVert_p\\le\\lVert f\\rVert_\\infty\\) for every exponent \\(p\\).\nThus the comparison consumes unit total measure, not a hypothesis\n\\(p\\ge1\\); this says nothing about whether the resulting quantity is a norm.",
